(3) All of the foregoing shall be required/inspected after receipt of a building permit application and before a building permit is issued for construction on the property. The planning committee shall have 30 days in which to review said application for determination of compliance with this article. If, during such review, the planning committee determines more information is necessary from the applicant, it may request, in writing, such information and mail such request, by certified mail, return receipt requested, to the applicant. Applicant shall furnish such requested information to the planning committee within ten days of receipt of said notice, and such information shall be deemed part of the application. During such review period, the planning committee may request the applicant to appear before the committee to answer any questions or supply further information concerning the matters set forth within the application. Likewise, during said review period, the applicant may request the planning committee to allow the applicant to appear before the planning committee in order to explain or comment upon any matters set forth in the application. It shall be solely within the discretion of the planning committee as whether to request or allow appearance of the applicant.
(b) Inspections and stop-work orders.
(1) The application or filing for a building permit shall be deemed to constitute the consent of the owner of the property described therein for the planning committee, or its designated representative, to include the city building inspector, to enter upon the property for the purposes of verifying the information contained within the application and to determine whether there has been compliance, during land-disturbing activity and/or construction or erection of improvements, with this article or with the plans submitted as part of the application.
(2) In the event the building inspector determines there is a failure to comply with this article or such plans, a stop-work order shall be issued by the building inspector and sent by certified mail, return receipt requested, to the owner of the property as disclosed on the application, and such order shall specify the act of noncompliance as found by the building inspector, and what acts must be taken by the owner to be in compliance with this article or such plans. Thereafter, the owner shall have 15 days in which to bring the property into compliance and until which no further work shall be done on the property except as may be necessary solely to bring the property into compliance with this article or such plans. The continuing of any work upon the property, after receipt of a stop-work order, and except as necessary to bring the property into compliance, shall be in violation of this article. Failure to bring the property into compliance within 15 days of receipt of such a stop-work order shall be a separate violation of this article.
